.TH BREWMASTER.PY 1 "2026-07-03" "2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brewmaster.py \- a smarter Homebrew upgrader with prefetch, retries, and logging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 brewmaster.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brewmaster.py
is an enhanced Homebrew upgrade wrapper that shows version diffs, prefetches
all downloads in parallel, retries failed packages individually with timeouts,
skips pinned packages, supports interactive per-package selection, and logs
every run to
.I ~/.brewmaster.log\c
\&.
.PP
Running without flags performs an interactive upgrade: it updates Homebrew
metadata (skipped automatically if updated within the last hour), lists all
outdated packages with version diffs, prompts for confirmation, prefetches
downloads in parallel, then upgrades each package individually — retrying
failures before reporting a summary.
.PP
The
.B brew
executable is resolved once to an absolute path; a warning is printed if it
lives outside the standard Homebrew locations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-approve all upgrades without an interactive prompt.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-interactive .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Show a numbered list and choose which packages to upgrade. Accepts
selections like
.BR 1,3,5\-7 ,
.BR all ,
or
.BR none .
Selection implies consent; no second confirmation prompt is shown.
.TP
.BR \-\-greedy " (default)"
Include auto-updating casks when checking for outdated packages.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-greedy
Disable greedy cask checking.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-only
Report outdated packages with version diffs and exit without upgrading.
Exits with status 3 if any outdated packages were found.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would be executed without running any of them.
Skips the confirmation prompt automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-skip " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Space-separated list of package names to exclude. Glob patterns are
supported via fnmatch:
.RS
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --skip node 'python@*'
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-formula\-only
Upgrade formulae only; skip all casks.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-cask\-only .
.TP
.B \-\-cask\-only
Upgrade casks only; skip all formulae.
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-formula\-only .
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a native macOS notification (via
.BR osascript )
when the run completes. Notification text is escaped to prevent AppleScript
injection.
.TP
.B \-\-backup
Before upgrading, dump the current Homebrew state to a timestamped Brewfile at
.IR ~/.brewmaster_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.Brewfile .
The five newest backups are kept; older ones are pruned. A failed dump prints
a warning and writes nothing.
Restore with:
.RS
.EX
brew bundle install --file=~/.brewmaster_backup_<timestamp>.Brewfile
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update
Skip
.B brew update
entirely.
.TP
.B \-\-force\-update
Run
.B brew update
even if it already ran within the last hour. By default the update step is
skipped when the Homebrew repository's FETCH_HEAD is less than an hour old.
.TP
.B \-\-sizes
Prefetch all downloads before the confirmation prompt and display the total
on-disk download size. Note: this downloads before you confirm.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-json
Append one structured JSON record per run (upgraded packages, failures,
elapsed time, exit code) to
.IR ~/.brewmaster_history.jsonl .
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Number of retry attempts per package when an upgrade fails or times out.
Default is
.BR 2 ,
minimum is
.BR 1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Timeout per package upgrade in seconds. Default is
.BR 600 .
A hung installer becomes a recorded failure instead of stalling the run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — nothing to do, or all upgrades succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (brew not found, non-interactive session without \-y, ...).
.TP
.B 2
Run completed but one or more packages failed.
.TP
.B 3
.B \-\-check\-only
found outdated packages.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl-C.
.SH FEATURES
.SS Parallel Download Prefetch
All bottles and casks are prefetched via
.B brew fetch
on a 4-worker thread pool before the sequential upgrade loop, so each
.B brew upgrade
hits the local cache.
.SS Smart Update Skipping
.B brew update
is skipped automatically when it ran within the last hour, saving the
slowest step of most runs.
.SS Security Hardening
Package names are validated against brew's naming alphabet before reaching
any subprocess. The log file is created with mode 0600. Every upgrade attempt
writes an AUDIT line with the exact command and exit code to the log.
.SS Pin Awareness
Reads
.B brew list --pinned
and automatically skips pinned formulae. If the pinned-package query fails, a
warning is printed and the run continues.
.SS Clean Interrupts and Cron Safety
Ctrl-C mid-upgrade prints how many packages were upgraded, failed, and not
attempted, then exits 130. In a non-TTY session without
.BR \-y ,
the tool exits 1 immediately instead of hanging on the prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive upgrade (default):
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py
.EE
.TP
Pick packages from a numbered list:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -i
.EE
.TP
Auto-approve, skip node and all python versions, notify:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -y --skip node 'python@*' --notify
.EE
.TP
Preview outdated packages (exit 3 if any found):
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --check-only
.EE
.TP
Show total download size before confirming:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --sizes
.EE
.TP
Backup bundle, then upgrade formulae only:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --backup --formula-only
.EE
.TP
Cron-friendly run with JSON history:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py -y --log-json
.EE
.TP
Give a slow cask 20 minutes before treating it as hung:
.EX
python3 brewmaster.py --cask-only --timeout 1200 -y
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster.log
Timestamped log of all runs with per-command AUDIT lines. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster_history.jsonl
One JSON record per run when
.B \-\-log\-json
is set. Mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.brewmaster_backup_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.Brewfile
Bundle snapshots created by
.BR \-\-backup ;
the five newest are kept.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later, Homebrew (
.I https://brew.sh
), macOS.
.PP
The
.B \-\-notify
flag requires
.B osascript
(available by default on macOS).
.PP
The
.B \-\-backup
flag requires the
.B brew-bundle
tap (included with Homebrew by default).
.SH AUTHOR
Anirban Bagchi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1)
